To fix the CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing) error in Next.js running on WordPress, follow these steps:

1. Install the `cors` middleware in your Next.js app by adding it to the top of your `pages/_app.js` file:

```javascript
import Cors from "cors";
import express from "express";
const cors = new Cors({ optionsSuccessStatus: 200 });

const app = express();

app.use(cors);

// ... The rest of your app setup goes here ...
```

2. In your `.htaccess` file, add the following lines to enable CORS requests:

```apache
RewriteEngine On
RewriteBase /
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ _next\/$1 [L]
Header set Access-Control-Allow-Credentials true
Header set Access-Control-Allow-Methods "GET,HEAD,PUT,POST,DELETE"
Header set Access-Control-Allow-Headers "Authorization"
```

3. In your WordPress site's `wp-config.php` file, add the following code to allow cross-origin requests:

```php
define('WP_ALLOW_RESPONSE_INCLUDES', true);
add_filter('rest_prevent_cors_x_requested_with_check', '__return_false');
add_action('init', function() {
    remove_action('rest_api_init', 'rest_enable_cors');
});
```

